## Backend: event-site-manager-service

**Repo path:** `F:/project_workspace/event-site-manager-service` (active REST API; not `malayalees-us-site-boot`).

### Entity changes (required for all new/changed entities)

```java
// ✅ DO
@GeneratedValue(strategy = GenerationType.SEQUENCE, generator = "sequenceGenerator")
@SequenceGenerator(
    name = "sequenceGenerator",
    sequenceName = "public.sequence_generator",
    allocationSize = 1
)

// ❌ DON'T — Hibernate default allocationSize = 50 conflicts with INCREMENT BY 1
@SequenceGenerator(name = "sequenceGenerator")
```

All ~78 domain entities under `src/main/java/com/eventsitemanager/domain/` use `allocationSize = 1`.

### Runtime sequence sync

| Component | Path | Role |
|-----------|------|------|
| `SequenceSynchronizationService` | `.../service/SequenceSynchronizationService.java` | `setval` on `sequence_generator` via static GREATEST list (matches SQL script) |
| `SequenceSynchronizationAspect` | `.../aop/sequence/SequenceSynchronizationAspect.java` | On duplicate PK: sync sequence and retry save |
| `AdminController` | `.../web/rest/AdminController.java` | `POST /api/admin/sync-sequence` |
| Duplicate-key pattern | [.cursor/rules/duplicate-key-prevention.mdc](mdc:../event-site-manager-service/.cursor/rules/duplicate-key-prevention.mdc) | Clear `entity.setId(null)` on create; AOP fallback |

### Schema alignment

When adding tables, update **both**:

1. End-of-schema `setval` GREATEST block in `Latest_Schema_Post__Blob_Claude_12.sql`
2. `sync_sequence_after_inserts.sql` and `SequenceSynchronizationService.java` GREATEST list

See [database_schema_guidelines.mdc](mdc:database_schema_guidelines.mdc).

### Known gap

Liquibase changelog `20250422000000_create_sequence_generator.xml` may still say `incrementBy="50"`. Fresh installs use canonical SQL schema (`INCREMENT BY 1`). Legacy envs: run `fix_sequence_generator_increment_by_one.sql` once.

